---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Design with intention">
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">A home design app for people planning their own place</span>
    <h1>Draw the plan. <em>Walk the room.</em> Render it real.</h1>
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p>Homely is a home design app for homeowners and DIY renovators, not a professional CAD tool. Sketch walls, rooms, doors, and windows on an accurate 2D plan, flip to a live 3D view of the exact same model, and queue a photorealistic render when you want to see it the way it will really look.</p>
      <div><a class="button" href="https://app.buildmy.house">Start designing your home ↗</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="plan-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span class="plan-mark-dot"></span></div>
  </section>
  <section class="cards" aria-label="Product highlights">
    <article class="card"><span class="number">01 / PLAN</span><h3>Sketch a real floor plan</h3><p>Draw walls, rooms, doors, and windows on a grid that keeps every measurement honest as you edit.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><span class="number">02 / 3D</span><h3>Step inside instantly</h3><p>Flip to a live 3D view of the same model, or split the screen and watch plan and 3D update together.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><span class="number">03 / RENDER</span><h3>Get a photoreal render</h3><p>Queue a path-traced render of your design — a finished image, not just an in-app preview.</p></article>
  </section>

  <section class="proof" aria-label="Screenshots of the app">
    <span class="eyebrow">The actual app, not a mockup</span>
    <h2>Here's what's really on screen.</h2>
    <p>Homely is still in late prototype — some of this UI will keep changing — but every screenshot below is a real capture of the working app, not a concept render.</p>

    <figure class="proof-main">
      <img
        src="/screenshots/v2-02-app-room-split.png"
        alt="Homely's split view showing a real room's 2D floor plan on the left and the matching live 3D view on the right"
        width="1600"
        height="1000"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>Plan and 3D, side by side, always in sync — a real room from the app.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="proof-grid">
      <figure>
        <img
          src="/screenshots/v2-04-app-3d-view.png"
          alt="Live 3D view of a room design, full screen, in the Homely app"
          width="1600"
          height="1000"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>The 3D view on its own.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img
          src="/screenshots/v2-05-app-catalog-panel.png"
          alt="Furniture catalog panel in the Homely app, showing items available to place in a room"
          width="1600"
          height="1000"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>The furniture catalog for filling out a room.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img
          src="/screenshots/v2-03-app-plan-view.png"
          alt="2D floor plan view in the Homely app, showing walls, rooms, and openings"
          width="1600"
          height="1000"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>The plan view on its own.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .proof {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin-top: 90px;
    padding-top: 70px;
  }
  .proof h2 {
    margin: 16px 0 20px;
  }
  .proof-main {
    margin: 50px 0 0;
  }
  .proof-main img {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    display: block;
    height: auto;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .proof-main figcaption {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
    font-size: .75rem;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .proof-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .proof-grid figure {
    margin: -1px 0 0 -1px;
  }
  .proof-grid img {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    display: block;
    height: auto;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .proof-grid figcaption {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
    font-size: .7rem;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .proof-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
